          %h2#in_constructive_mathematics In constructive mathematics
          %p
            The given proof of the inverse function theorem above relies on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mean+value+theorem"} mean value theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            is only true for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+differentiable+functions"} uniformly differentiable functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mean+value+theorem"} mean value theorem
            and could prove the inverse function theorem for continuously differentiable functions.
          %h2#as_an_axiom_for_archimedean_ordered_fields  As an axiom for Archimedean ordered fields
          %p
            While
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuously+differentiable+functions"} continuously differentiable functions
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+uniformly+differentiable+functions"} locally uniformly differentiable functions
            are well-defined in every
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archimedean+ordered+field"} Archimedean ordered field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For any Archimedean ordered field
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %strong continuously differentiable inverse function axiom
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                states that given any differentiable function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
